00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:44.929
there are a few things that I want to explain

19
00:00:44.929 --> 00:00:49.490
about the empty open world map and why it's so important

20
00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:50.950
and the first thing is the grid.

21
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:55.109
So the grid is the term that we use

22
00:00:55.109 --> 00:00:57.750
to describe our streaming grid

23
00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:01.869
and this grid controls where assets are seen

24
00:01:01.869 --> 00:01:03.649
and more importantly, where they're not seen.

25
00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:08.650
So when we create our world using the open world template

26
00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.950
we're already gonna have our world set up

27
00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.209
to make use of this grid

28
00:01:14.209 --> 00:01:18.489
and the grid works by loading in the different cells

29
00:01:18.489 --> 00:01:21.129
and you can see the cells marked here

30
00:01:21.129 --> 00:01:24.430
when this loading range approaches them

31
00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.030
or gets further away from them

32
00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:28.370
and this loading range is actually connected

33
00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:30.250
to our character.

34
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.250
So we have a streaming source

35
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.769
and in many instances it is going to be the character

36
00:01:34.769 --> 00:01:37.670
and the streaming source defines

37
00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:40.849
the more or less the center of your world

38
00:01:40.849 --> 00:01:43.969
and then as your player progresses throughout the world,

39
00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:46.409
the streaming source is going to allow things

40
00:01:46.409 --> 00:01:49.969
to be streamed in and streamed out.

41
00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:52.689
So that's one of the reasons why we wanna come up here

42
00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:55.670
and make sure that we've gone up to file new level

43
